// Settings browser catalog: one CFG_ITEM row per setting of cfg_root (Emu/system_config.h), in the PC dialog's order
// (tab by tab, section by section: the order of the rows on a browser page), then CFG_VALUE rows (the PC text of a value).
// Edited by hand; ps4-port/tools/gen_cfg_catalog.py --check and ps4-port/tests/cfg_browser_test.cpp check it against the tree.
//
// CFG_ITEM(key, tab, section, class, label, help, reason, tip, editor, step, coarse, unit, values, value reason, depends, scope, flags)
//   key      node names joined with " > " (the key of the pins and of startup.log)
//   tab      cpu gpu audio io system network advanced emulator debug (ps4 holds the port's switches, no rows here)
//   class    E expose, W warning on the first change, U unavailable on PS4 (greyed, reason), H hidden (no effect on PS4)
//   reason   why W / U / H (count_ = none); tip = the PC tooltip id (count_ = none)
//   editor   auto_ (from the cfg type) or a special editor (ps4_cfg_catalog.hpp)
//   step     Left/Right step and the R1 step (0 = 1 and 10); unit is shown after a number
//   values   "X" allowed, "~X" warning, "-X" greyed, "#X" not offered, "a..b" numeric range; empty = all
//   depends  "key=value[|value]" or "key!=value", '&' separated: the row is dimmed until it holds
//   scope    both, global_only (PC: disk cache) or game_only (PC: game speed, 3D)
//   flags    F_NONE, F_HOME (the in-game menu edits it), F_NO_DEFAULT (random default, never reset)
// CFG_VALUE(key, YAML spelling, label id, text): the label of one value (count_ = the text, the same in every language)


